BT 14 TL 56 780 Td
/F2 15 Tf (Assessment tasks aligned to outcomes) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (For students, the assessment is the real curriculum. They look at what will be assessed) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (and learn that. This effect of assessment on learning is called backwash.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (Backwash is usually discussed as a problem, but in an aligned course it becomes a) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (strength. If the assessment task requires the verb of the outcome, then preparing for) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (the assessment is the same thing as learning what was intended. Students who study "for) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (the exam" study the right thing.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (An aligned assessment task has two features. First, it requires the performance named in) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (the outcome: to assess "apply", students must apply; to assess "explain", they must) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (explain in their own words. Second, it is graded with criteria that describe quality of) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (performance, not with marks counted for separate remembered points.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (Oral examination, projects, portfolios, case analyses and problem solving are easier to) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (align with high-level outcomes than multiple-choice tests of recall. A test of recall is) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (aligned only with outcomes of recall.) Tj T*
