/F2 15 Tf (Common mistakes and a short checklist) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (Mistake 1. Alignment is confused with coverage. A course can cover every topic and still) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (be misaligned, because alignment is about verbs, not about the list of topics.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (Mistake 2. Outcomes are written after the course is designed, only for the official) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (documents. Then they do not guide anything.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (Mistake 3. Only the examination is changed. If students never practise the performance) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (during the course, a demanding examination is unfair.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (Mistake 4. Too many outcomes with vague verbs such as "know" and "understand".) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (Checklist for a teacher.) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (- Does every outcome contain an observable verb at the intended level?) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (- For every outcome, is there an activity in which students themselves perform the verb?) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (- Does every assessment task require the same verb?) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (- Are grading criteria written as levels of quality of the performance?) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (- Would a student who only memorised the slides fail the assessment? If not, the course) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (still rewards surface learning.) Tj T*
ET
