/F2 15 Tf (Prestructural and unistructural answers) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (Take the question "Why does it become dark at night?") Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (A prestructural answer: "Because it is night" or "Because we need to sleep". The student) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (uses words related to the question but shows no relevant knowledge. Tautology, denial) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (and irrelevant personal association are typical signs.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (A unistructural answer: "Because the Sun goes to the other side of the Earth". One) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (relevant fact is selected. It is correct as far as it goes, but the student stops there) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (and cannot say more when asked.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (Unistructural answers are common after rote learning: the student has memorised a) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (definition or a formula and reproduces exactly one element. Typical verbs at this level) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (are "identify", "name", "recall" and "follow a simple procedure".) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (A unistructural answer should not be dismissed. It is the starting point of) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (understanding. But a course whose assessment can be passed with unistructural answers) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (teaches students that naming things is enough.) Tj T*
ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 290 40 Td (13) Tj ET
endstream
