/F2 15 Tf (Relational answers: the qualitative shift) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (A relational answer: "The Earth rotates around its axis, so each place is turned towards) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (the Sun for part of the rotation and away from it for the rest. When our side faces) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (away, sunlight does not reach us directly, and that is night. One full rotation takes) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (about 24 hours, which is why day and night repeat with that period.") Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (Now the facts form a mechanism. Each element has a function in the explanation, and the) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (student can answer "why" and "how" questions within the topic. The answer to "what if) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (the Earth rotated twice as slowly?" follows directly: days and nights would be twice as) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (long.) Tj T*
